{"type":"assistant","uuid":"dddd7949-375a-4559-8246-5152e90e9439","session_id":"b9b7f547-97a1-4843-b060-6a58b94cfa1d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"dddd7949-375a-4559-8246-5152e90e9439","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the issue clearly. The `LocalLinkMovementMethod` class is the root cause. When a user long-presses on a URL:\n\n1. `ACTION_DOWN` is received → it selects the link text\n2. The long-press gesture is detected → context menu appears\n3. `ACTION_UP` is received → it calls `link[0].onClick(widget)`, opening the URL\n\nThe fix should prevent `onClick` from being called when the gesture was a long press. \n\nThe standard Android approach for this in `LinkMovementMethod` (the framework class) is to call `Touch.onTouchEvent` which handles this internally. \n\nLooking at the actual implementation, I see that `LocalLinkMovementMethod` only delegates to `Touch.onTouchEvent` when no link exists at the touch point, which is why it bypasses the long-press detection logic that would normally prevent the click from firing. The cleanest solution is to track whether a long press was detected during the gesture.\n\nI need to add a boolean flag and check `isLongPressed()` in `ACTION_DOWN` to set it, then skip the click handler in `ACTION_UP` if that flag was true. This way, the long-press context menu can display without also triggering the link click. The `LinkMovementMethod` already has the `isLongpressed()` check built in, so this approach aligns with how Android's standard touch handling works.\n\nNow I'm checking which imports are available—I already have the MotionEvent import, so I can proceed with the implementation. Then I'll build and test to verify the fix works correctly.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"6abd3a4d-83dd-4049-b749-0e53e1a4afce","session_id":"b9b7f547-97a1-4843-b060-6a58b94cfa1d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"6abd3a4d-83dd-4049-b749-0e53e1a4afce","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've identified the root cause. The `LocalLinkMovementMethod` class handles `ACTION_DOWN` and `ACTION_UP` events for links, but it doesn't account for long-press gestures. When a user long-presses a URL:\n1. `ACTION_DOWN` fires → the link gets selected\n2. Long press gesture is detected → context menu appears\n3. `ACTION_UP` fires → it still calls `link[0].onClick(widget)`, opening the URL\n\nThe standard Android `LinkMovementMethod` delegates to `Touch.onTouchEvent` which handles this internally. But `LocalLinkMovementMethod` overrides this behavior and only calls `Touch.onTouchEvent` when there's no link at the touch point.\n\nThe fix: track whether a long-press was detected and skip the `onClick()` call in `ACTION_UP` if it was.\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"23d1a2e6-2cd3-4882-a331-857e311a2613","session_id":"b9b7f547-97a1-4843-b060-6a58b94cfa1d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"23d1a2e6-2cd3-4882-a331-857e311a2613","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b63b1fc7e6e32a6a","name":"edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/antu_shared/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/qwen_original_run2/bug-114/app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/LocalLinkMovementMethod.java","old_string":"/**\n * Copied from http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8558732\n */\npublic class LocalLinkMovementMethod extends LinkMovementMethod {\n    static LocalLinkMovementMethod sInstance;\n\n    public static LocalLinkMovementMethod getInstance() {\n        if (sInstance == null)\n            sInstance = new LocalLinkMovementMethod();\n\n        return sInstance;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public boolean onTouchEvent(TextView widget, Spannable buffer, MotionEvent event) {\n        int action = event.getAction();\n\n        if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_UP ||\n                action == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN) {\n            int x = (int) event.getX();\n            int y = (int) event.getY();\n\n            x -= widget.getTotalPaddingLeft();\n            y -= widget.getTotalPaddingTop();\n\n            x += widget.getScrollX();\n            y += widget.getScrollY();\n\n            Layout layout = widget.getLayout();\n            int line = layout.getLineForVertical(y);\n            int off = layout.getOffsetForHorizontal(line, x);\n\n            ClickableSpan[] link = buffer.getSpans(off, off, ClickableSpan.class);\n\n            if (link.length != 0) {\n                if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_UP) {\n                    link[0].onClick(widget);\n                } else if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN) {\n                    Selection.setSelection(buffer,\n                            buffer.getSpanStart(link[0]),\n                            buffer.getSpanEnd(link[0]));\n                }\n\n                return true;\n            } else {\n                Selection.removeSelection(buffer);\n                Touch.onTouchEvent(widget, buffer, event);\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n        return Touch.onTouchEvent(widget, buffer, event);\n    }\n}","new_string":"/**\n * Copied from http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8558732\n */\npublic class LocalLinkMovementMethod extends LinkMovementMethod {\n    static LocalLinkMovementMethod sInstance;\n\n    private boolean mLongPressed = false;\n\n    public static LocalLinkMovementMethod getInstance() {\n        if (sInstance == null)\n            sInstance = new LocalLinkMovementMethod();\n\n        return sInstance;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public boolean onTouchEvent(TextView widget, Spannable buffer, MotionEvent event) {\n        int action = event.getAction();\n\n        if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_UP ||\n                action == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN) {\n            int x = (int) event.getX();\n            int y = (int) event.getY();\n\n            x -= widget.getTotalPaddingLeft();\n            y -= widget.getTotalPaddingTop();\n\n            x += widget.getScrollX();\n            y += widget.getScrollY();\n\n            Layout layout = widget.getLayout();\n            int line = layout.getLineForVertical(y);\n            int off = layout.getOffsetForHorizontal(line, x);\n\n            ClickableSpan[] link = buffer.getSpans(off, off, ClickableSpan.class);\n\n            if (link.length != 0) {\n                if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_UP) {\n                    if (!mLongPressed) {\n                        link[0].onClick(widget);\n                    }\n                    mLongPressed = false;\n                } else if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN) {\n                    mLongPressed = false;\n                    Selection.setSelection(buffer,\n                            buffer.getSpanStart(link[0]),\n                            buffer.getSpanEnd(link[0]));\n                }\n\n                return true;\n            } else {\n                mLongPressed = false;\n                Selection.removeSelection(buffer);\n                Touch.onTouchEvent(widget, buffer, event);\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Reset on other event types (CANCEL, MOVE, etc.)\n        if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_CANCEL) {\n            mLongPressed = false;\n        }\n        return Touch.onTouchEvent(widget, buffer, event);\n    }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":27280,"output_tokens":1436,"cache_read_input_tokens":23056,"total_tokens":28716}}}
